<!DOCTYPE airframe SYSTEM "../airframe.dtd">
<airframe name="Easystar3_black">
  <description>
    Basic fixedwing airframe equipped with flightcontroller hardware

    + MODEL:        Multiplex Easystar III Yellow edition
    + FC:           Lisa MX v2.1
    + ACTUATORS:    Default of set MS-12020-MG
    + GNSS          uBlox M10
    + IMU           Default Aspirin v2.1 
    + MAGNETOMETER: QMC5883L on GNSS module
    + ESC:          Default of set ROXXY BL-Control 720 S-BEC ESC
    + RCRX:         OpenRXSR Receiver
    + AIRSPEED:     Sensirion SDP33
    + BARO          MS5611 on FC
    + TELEMETRY:    SiK 868MHz modem
    + CURRENT:      N/A
    + RANGEFINDER:  VB50A
    + MOTOR:        Default of set ROXXY BL Outrunner C28-30 1100Kv
    + PROPPELLER:   Default Foldable 7" x 6" two bladed

    NOTES:
    + Servo pins point to aft(tail) of airframe
    + SBus output on receiver MUST modified to have un-inverted output, this F4 cannot do it in software
      This is done by soldering the RX SBus output wire on pad B of the RCRX
    + Servos powered via BEC of ESC outputs 5.0V
    + Flightcontroller powered via servo rail
    + JP8 Closed and JP9 Opened so on UART5_VCC is V_IN, thus 5V to RCRX
    + Telemetry modem powered via V/GND pins of UART on FC
    + Uploading of the firmware via SWD (useing a BlackMagicProbe debug adapter)
    + A GNSS device with QMC8553L magneto on the same PCB
    + GNSS set to ~13Hz update rate, 3 constelations, SBAS enabled
    + Advised battery for this airframe is a 1500mAh 3S LiPo min. 30C
    + If testing "Classic" (as in not ETECS..) make sure to disable the settings/estimation/ac_char
    + One could set the USE_AIRSPEED value to FALSE at first, for no airspeed tests
    + Make sure v7.0 or higher of PPRZ autopilot release is used
  </description>

